# Real, confirmed reason this exists: trixie's current kernel
# (1:6.18.34-1+rpt1, verified via archive.raspberrypi.com's live trixie
# Packages index) is too new for nexmon's brcmfmac-nexmon-dkms package
# (built/validated by Kali against the 6.12 line - confirmed compile
# failure: del_timer_sync/from_timer implicit-declaration errors and
# cfg80211_ops incompatible-pointer-type errors against 6.18.34).
# archive.raspberrypi.com's bookworm suite (still actively maintained,
# NOT abandoned - verified live, same day as this comment) currently
# serves 1:6.12.93-1+rpt1 for these exact packages, which is in the
# validated-compatible range.
#
# Scoped to ONLY the kernel image/header packages, from ONLY this
# specific origin+suite - this is not a distribution-wide downgrade.
# See go-port/docs/kernel-nexmon-compatibility.md for the full evidence
# trail (exact apt-cache madison/policy output, not just this summary).
#
# Real, confirmed CI finding: priority 990 was NOT enough. Per
# apt_preferences(5), priority in (500,990] "causes a version to be
# installed unless ... the installed version is more recent" - since
# pi-gen's stage0 already installs trixie's newer 6.18.34 kernel BEFORE
# this stage runs, 990 left apt-cache policy's own Candidate: on
# 6.18.34 despite bookworm's 6.12.93 correctly showing priority 990 in
# the version table. Only priority >1000 ("install even if this
# constitutes a downgrade") actually forces the downgrade.
Package: linux-image-* linux-headers-*
Pin: release o=Raspberry Pi Foundation, n=bookworm
Pin-Priority: 1001
